586	\begin{proof}
587		A uniformly random $x \in V$ has independent components $x^{(i)}$, each uniformly distributed in $V^{(i)}$. Hence the pair $(L(x), R(x)) = \bigl( (L^{(i)}(x^{(i)}))_{i=1}^m,\, (R^{(i)}(x^{(i)}))_{i=1}^m \bigr)$ is distributed exactly as the product of the distributions $\mu_{L^{(i)},\,R^{(i)}}$ for $i = 1, 2, \dots, m$.
588	\end{proof}
